yes, the game should somehow require a strategic attitude adjustment.

at first you should have to get tougher to survive (ala rogue).  then
at some point you should have to get wiser to survive.  monsters should
not just get tougher (the mega-troll hits, yawn ...) but they should
get craftier.  there should be more attacks on your magic so you don't
get complacent about it.  also the attacks should be structured more
to put you at a disadvantage but not necessarily kill you outright.
you would then have to devise methods of overcoming the disadvantages
without resorting to the unispired strategy of getting a super-weapon
and killing everything in 2 or 3 hits.  of course, if you get too
disadvantaged without remedies then you may be in grave danger ...

